Mesa on LikeOS with the display-manager device.

The first port patch declared LikeOS a POSIX system without KMS/DRM, which
was true at the time.  The kernel now carries a display-manager interface
(/dev/dri/card0, /dev/dri/renderD128, the vmwgfx ioctl set) and a
sysfs-style device tree, and libdrm is built.  So:

 - meson.build: `likeos' joins the systems that have KMS/DRM, which turns
   on the drm DRI platform, DRI3 presentation, libgbm and the vmwgfx
   winsys, exactly as on the reference system.
 - src/loader/loader.c: the fast PCI-id lookup reads
   /sys/dev/char/MAJ:MIN/device/{vendor,device}; the tree serves those.
 - src/gallium/winsys/svga/drm/pb_buffer_simple_fenced.c: sched_yield()
   while draining fences, as on every other POSIX system.
 - src/util/detect_os.h: the comment no longer claims there is no DRM.

